Hi,

after some (middly subtile) hints in RGRN I tried one MR free character.

Here is the story of Bestar the chaotic human barbarian with various 
sexes, but first some precautious thoughts.


So what to expect without MR?

The first few dungeon levels obviously nothing unusual. But below DL8 
you have to deal with polytraps thus there is the need of either =oPC 
or "oUC or a nice collection of spare body armor.
The next danger comes from tele especially leveltele traps. So TC is
recommended. (And a whole lot of searching before ;-)

Later (if you destroyed/used the polytraps) the problem of magic using 
monsters (Golden Naga, * Lich, Titan, * Priest, Angel, Archon) arises.
There is destroy armor, touch of death and the devastating magic 
attacks of A's and Priests.
You can't prevent destroy armor, but you can maintain a distance 
between the aggressor and you. The same goes for the other magic 
attacks besides the touch of death. So /oT and /oDig are a must.

But because some of your armor will get destroyed you need spare parts 
and don't waste ?oEA on consumption material.

The touch of death is a special case, since it's an instant killer you 
need good means against it.
There is amongst others wear an "oLS and come with an instakill weapon 
or walk around undead.

Now what character to choose?
First the Quest Artifact should not provide MR (BHPRaRoSV)and the 
character should come with builtin firepower (BSV).
Samurais are lawful, Valks (LN) have a too heavy quest artifact so I  
chose a chaotic barbarian.

Enough with the intro.


